SUMMARY:AYPROS Leadership & Service: Asheville Humane Society Enrichment B
 uild
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\n**⚠️ IMPORTANT: Re
 gistration Required**\nTo reserve your spot\, you MUST register through th
 e official AYPROS event page: https://aypros.wildapricot.org/event-6874118
 \n\nRSVPing on Meetup does not reserve your spot. Space is limited to just
  12 volunteers\, and registrations will be counted through AYPROS only.\n\
 n**Help us make shelter life a little brighter for Asheville's animals! 
 🐾**\nJoin AYPROS for an afternoon of volunteering at Asheville Humane S
 ociety! We'll roll up our sleeves and help assemble enrichment items for s
 helter animals\, including dogs\, cats\, and small animals.\nThese enrichm
 ent activities\, including treats and toys\, help reduce stress\, anxiety\
 , and boredom while supporting the animals' mental and behavioral well-bei
 ng during their time at the shelter.\nVolunteers will work together to pre
 pare enrichment items for distribution and may assist with other tasks dep
 ending on the shelter's needs.\n\n**Event Details**\n\n* **Date:** Friday\
 , October 23\, 2026\n* **Time:** 2:00–4:00 PM\n* **Location:** Asheville
  Humane Society\, 14 Forever Friend Lane\, Asheville\, NC 28806\n* **Regis
 tration:** Free \\| Limited to 12 volunteers\n*\n\n**What to Know Before Y
 ou Go**\n\n* **Arrival & Waivers:** Please arrive on time! All volunteers 
 must complete a waiver before participating. Waivers will be available to 
 fill out on-site for participants ages 18 and older.\n* **What to wear:** 
 Long pants and closed-toe shoes are required.\n* **Where to meet:** Head t
 o the Humane Society Adoption Center (the building on the left). The educa
 tion room door will be open\, and staff will greet volunteers there.\n* **
 What to expect:** A hands-on volunteer experience assembling enrichment it
 ems\, with additional tasks possible depending on the shelter's needs.\n*\
 n\n**Want to Give a Little Extra?**\nAsheville Humane Society also welcome
 s donations of items used in its enrichment program! Some wishlist items i
 nclude canned pumpkin (not pie filling)\, xylitol-free applesauce\, dog tr
 eats\, fleece blankets\, rolled oats\, and peanut butter powder.\n\nDonati
 ons are completely optional and can be brought with you on the day of the 
 event.\n\n**Only 12 volunteer spots are available\, so register early to j
 oin us!**\n\nWe hope you'll join us for an afternoon of giving back and co
 nnecting with fellow young professionals while supporting animals in our c
 ommunity.
